WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.089
In chapter 907 of One Piece, we first learn
about an infamous pirate called Rocks D. Xebec.

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:10.140
Since that chapter, we’ve learned that he
not only tried to take over the world, but

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:14.620
he was also the captain of a crew that included
three future Emperors.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:20.070
So in this video, we are going to explain
everything that we know for a fact, all the

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:25.012
hints about his past, and even some incredible
speculations about his true purpose in the

00:00:25.012 --> 00:00:26.012
story.

00:00:26.012 --> 00:00:31.119
Now since we really don’t know a whole lot
about Rocks, it is important to clearly explain

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:34.470
what is fact, or close to fact, and what is
speculation.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:39.059
To do that we are going to break up the information
about Rocks into six categories and in each

00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:42.380
category discuss what we know and what we
can speculate.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.550
Starting with a brief introduction.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:50.460
In chapter 907, Luffy’s grandfather Garp
first revealed that the Rocks pirates ruled

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:56.609
the seas forty years ago, which is about fourteen
years before Gol D. Roger became the pirate

00:00:56.609 --> 00:00:57.609
king.

00:00:57.609 --> 00:01:01.980
Garp tells a group of marines that if the
Rocks pirates were to reform then they would

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:06.720
be a threat beyond what any of them could
imagine.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.759
Fifty chapters later, the former fleet admiral
Sengoku reveals a boatload more about Rocks

00:01:11.759 --> 00:01:13.870
and his insane crew.

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:18.350
We learned that the World Government considered
Rocks to be their biggest threat and it took

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:25.650
an unbelievable effort to stop him from taking
over the world, which we’ll discuss more

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:26.650
later on.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:32.660
So let’s dive into what was probably the
strongest pirate crew ever.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:33.740
Here are the facts.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:38.570
On this ridiculous crew were three future
Emperors of the Sea: The strongest creature

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:45.030
in the world, Kaido, the monstrous mother
Big Mom, and former strongest man in the world,

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:46.030
Whitebeard.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:50.610
Besides these three powerhouses, we have Shiki,
who was a former rival of Roger’s.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:56.350
In addition, this old lady, Miss Bakkin, was
part of the crew before she joined the science

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.000
group, MADS.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.600
Then we have Silver Axe, who is a complete
mystery.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:09.350
Captain John, who had a famous treasure, died,
and then unfortunately got turned into a zombie

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.819
on Thriller Ba.

00:02:10.819 --> 00:02:14.530
And finally there was Wang Zhi, also known
as Ochoku.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:19.510
While we don’t know a lot about Ochoku,
we do know he ruled over the Rocks’ pirates

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:21.560
former base island.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:26.349
And we cannot mention a pirate crew without
discussing their sh.

00:02:26.349 --> 00:02:32.030
While we don’t have any other information
about it, you can see that it is a large vessel

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:33.950
and pretty damn intimidating.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:40.870
Now, let’s shift to discussing the relationships
of this wild crew because it is unlike anything

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:42.800
we have seen in the story.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:48.830
In chapter 957, Sengoku revealed that the
crew’s dynamic was horribly toxic.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:52.690
The crew members would regularly fight and
even kill each other.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:57.310
But what is even more interesting is what
we can speculate about the crew’s relationships

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.570
from other clues sprinkled throughout the
story.

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:05.450
First, Whitebeard seemed to have a very negative
experience on Rocks’ crew.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.060
His reaction was kinda like a boss you hate
to work for.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:15.090
In chapter 964, Whitebeard initially refuses
to let the samurai Oden join his crew because

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:20.310
Whitebeard had a bad experience with his own
previous crew, which was most likely the Rocks

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:21.500
pirates.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:25.700
From this we can assume that he has a lot
of resentment from his time on Rocks’ crew

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.750
since it is still bothering him decades later.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:34.640
He must have learned that having too many
strong willed personalities can destroy a

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:35.640
crew.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:44.060
This supports Sengoku’s claims that the
crew was in a state of near constant chaos.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:47.670
Another fact is that Big Mom did not trust
Rocks at all.

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:52.610
In chapter 1041 during a flashback, we see
that Kaido has just joined the Rocks crew.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:58.800
And Big Mom tells Kaido that if he needed
anything, he should count on her because Rocks

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.290
was not trustworthy.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:06.230
From this, it seems that Rocks did not lead
by inspiring trust and loyalty, as it seems

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:10.150
that many of them did not even like him at
all.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:15.370
And this mistrust had the ultimate consequence
for Rocks, when the crew later abandoned him

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.380
as we’ll discuss later on.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:23.620
If this is true, then we have to wonder how
exactly Rocks kept this crazy crew together.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:29.470
Let’s shift over and dive into everything
we know about Rocks D. Xebec as a person as

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:31.480
well as his powers and history.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:36.030
Of course, starting with the fact that he
is dead… **coughs** maybe.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:40.630
Even though Sengoku tells us that Rocks is
dead, the circumstances of his mysterious

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:46.600
disappearance make me believe that this is
not all we have seen from such an important

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:47.600
character.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:51.270
And let’s compare this situation to an equally
famous dead pirate.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:56.520
The execution of Roger is the first scene
in the entire story, and while we don’t

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:02.979
learn a lot more about Roger until much later
on, his influence is present all throughout

00:05:02.979 --> 00:05:03.979
the story.

00:05:03.979 --> 00:05:08.389
From his former crew mates, his rivals, and
even the fact that we found clues about his

00:05:08.389 --> 00:05:10.580
journey along the way.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:18.669
But while Rocks was pretty much an equally
powerful and influential figure, we did not

00:05:18.669 --> 00:05:22.760
learn anything about him for over 900 chapters.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:29.150
So it makes me think that one, he is either
still alive and going to play a role in the

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:35.590
story, or two, he is dead, but we will get
a huge reveal about his past in the upcoming

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:36.590
arcs.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:40.970
Previously on this channel we have even discussed
the possibility that he might have been Luffy’s

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:45.819
other Grandfather, or another theory by the
creator Artur speculates that he could actually

00:05:45.819 --> 00:05:50.650
be the secret ruler of the world, Imu.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:54.940
Taking over the world was Rocks’ goal in
the first place and these two characters were

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:58.300
introduced so close together in the story.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:05.139
But whether he is dead or alive, we can reasonably
assume that he was evil.

00:06:05.139 --> 00:06:10.400
We know that Garp and Roger, both of whom
are “good” characters, tried to stop him

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.940
from achieving his goals.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:16.620
Also, Whitebeard clearly didn’t like him
and the World Government considered the Rocks

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:17.750
Pirates terrorists.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:26.000
So whatever his true intentions were, it is
likely that he committed terrible acts in

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.759
the pursuit of his dreams.

00:06:27.759 --> 00:06:29.550
And what were his dreams?

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:34.530
Well, we are told by Sengoku that Rocks was
ambitious and his dream was to be King of

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:35.530
the World.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:40.930
And damn that’s a title we have basically
never heard anyone use before.

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:46.740
Not only did he want to become pirate king
like Luffy, it seems he truly wanted to dominate

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:50.180
and rule over everyone.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:55.230
And he almost succeeded, which we will discuss
during his final battle later on.

00:06:55.230 --> 00:07:01.280
This leads to another interesting question,
can someone be king of the world without being

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.320
insanely powerful?

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:09.310
We know that it took both Roger and Garp teaming
up to defeat Rocks, and he was considered

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:11.560
the former pirate kings’ greatest rival.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.870
So clearly he was a strong fighter.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:19.700
We know that Rocks used a sword, as we are
shown in this scene.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:24.560
Even Kaido considered Rocks to be one of the
few pirates who could give him a challenge.

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:31.530
And since we also know that Kaido, Big Mom,
and Whitebeard all had conqueror’s haki,

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:37.560
it makes sense that their former captain would
as well.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:42.599
This is speculation, but his conqueror’s
haki could also have been on another level,

00:07:42.599 --> 00:07:44.090
since he commanded them.

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:48.530
This is further supported because his main
goal was to be king of the world.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:54.610
And if that’s not legendary conqueror’s
spirit, then I don’t know what is.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:08:00.470
One thing we have no details about is if Rocks
had a devil fruit.

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:05.600
There is no mention of such powers, so it
is possible he did not have a devil fruit,

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.860
similar to Roger and Garp.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:11.610
Or he might have had one and we just haven’t
been told yet.

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:15.909
Another possibility that we can speculate
is that Rocks was patiently waiting to get

00:08:15.909 --> 00:08:21.819
the right fruit – sound like anyone familiar
– and that Rocks was finally going to get

00:08:21.819 --> 00:08:25.139
that devil fruit during the legendary battle
we will discuss in a moment.

00:08:25.139 --> 00:08:31.139
And alongside his powers, Rocks was deeply
curious about history.

00:08:31.139 --> 00:08:35.110
Sengoku tells us that he broke many of the
world’s taboos and that he was erased from

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:38.159
history because of it.

00:08:38.159 --> 00:08:44.459
This must mean that he was researching the
poneglyphs, which are these unbreakable stones

00:08:44.459 --> 00:08:47.990
that tell the history of the void century.

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:52.170
Throughout the story, researching the poneglyphs
is the only reason the world government has

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:58.279
erased a group of people, such as on the island
of Ohara and as they are trying to do to the

00:08:58.279 --> 00:09:01.100
government scientist, Dr. Vegapunk, in the
current arc.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:05.290
And this allows us to speculate that either
Rocks himself could read the poneglyphs or

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:08.130
that he knew someone who could.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:11.860
This idea opens a whole new avenue for theories.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:16.360
For example, one interesting theory centers
around the mysterious three-eyed tribe which

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.800
was first mentioned in chapter 853.

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:23.510
During the whole cake island arc, we meet
Big Mom’s daughter, Pudding.

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:28.339
She was born with a third eye, meaning that
her father must have been from the three-eyed

00:09:28.339 --> 00:09:29.339
tribe.

00:09:29.339 --> 00:09:34.230
According to Big Mom, people from this tribe
naturally possess the ability to use the Voice

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:35.230
of All Things.

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:41.440
Though in Pudding’s case, she has not awakened
the power yet.

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:46.230
This mysterious power allows certain people
to hear the thoughts of animals such as the

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:50.860
sea kings and even vaguely understand the
words on the poneglyphs.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:55.850
But how does Big Mom know about this tribe
in the first place?

00:09:55.850 --> 00:10:01.010
These are all speculation, but a simple, though
unlikely answer, is that she could have randomly

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:04.340
found them on an island somewhere in the world.

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:13.370
But we have never seen this tribe anywhere
and very few people seem to know they exist.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:20.100
Another possibility is that Rocks himself
was from the three eye tribe or that he had

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:23.210
someone on the crew who was.

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:27.730
This would explain how he could research the
history of the void century since only two

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:30.870
people are confirmed to be able to read the
poneglyphs.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:35.200
Kaido also knows of the secret ability of
the three eye tribe, so he could have also

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.089
learned it from Rocks.

00:10:37.089 --> 00:10:44.390
It would also make sense that they learned
about the poneglyphs from Rocks, since we

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:48.300
are never told that either of them traveled
to Lodestar island.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:53.639
In chapter 820, we are told that it is on
Lodestar that a person is supposed to first

00:10:53.639 --> 00:10:55.730
learn about the poneglyphs.

00:10:55.730 --> 00:11:00.589
But moving back to some facts, Rocks was also
a member of the D clan.

00:11:00.589 --> 00:11:05.360
People who have this initial, such as Luffy,
Blackbeard, and Dragon, are said to be the

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:08.070
enemies of the celestial dragons.

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:14.780
It would make sense then that he was also
likely a charismatic leader, similar to Luffy,

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:20.250
and he somehow convinced all of these strong
pirates to come together to make one big score.

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:26.390
And that one big score seems to be taking
out the celestial dragons on the legendary

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:28.139
island, God Valley.

00:11:28.139 --> 00:11:33.639
And you can also land one big score by subscribing
to the channel to receive more videos just

00:11:33.639 --> 00:11:34.690
like this one.

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:41.380
So let’s finally discuss what happened in
the legendary battle on God Valley where Rocks

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:42.380
was defeated.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:48.440
First, we know that 38 years ago the Rocks
pirates attacked a mysterious island called

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:49.940
God Valley.

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:55.560
This event has been covered up by the World
Government because basically no one knows

00:11:55.560 --> 00:12:01.130
about it, except for people who were there
or older marines.

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:05.130
Part of the reason it was covered up is the
fact that Rocks could only be stopped by an

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:13.180
alliance between a much younger Garp and Roger
before he became pirate king.

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:15.960
And what a clash it must have been.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:16.960
Rocks.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:17.960
Roger.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:18.960
Whitebeard.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:19.960
Garp.

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:20.960
Big Mom.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:21.960
Kaido.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:25.350
**praying hands** Please Oda-sensei, show
us more of this legendary fight.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:30.470
And while we know next to nothing about the
actual battle or the island itself – which

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:36.730
has vanished – we are told that Garp and
Roger defended the celestial dragons and their

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:39.690
slaves who were on the island.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:42.649
But part of this does not make any sense.

00:12:42.649 --> 00:12:47.610
You see, we know that Garp hates the celestial
dragons and he has even refused to become

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:51.580
an admiral because he doesn’t want to take
orders from them.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:57.529
So we have to wonder why he and Roger saved
the celestial dragons on God Valley.

00:12:57.529 --> 00:13:03.060
There are a few options, and the last one
will completely blow your mind.

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:08.060
But first, the easiest possibility is that
Garp simply protected the slaves on God Valley.

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:10.220
Certainly that would fit with Garp’s character.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:15.070
Another option that I’ve theorized in a
separate video, is that Garp, Roger, and Rocks

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:18.779
were all once on a crew together before Rocks
went power-crazy.

00:13:18.779 --> 00:13:25.940
So perhaps Garp and Roger felt it was their
duty to stop Rocks before he did something

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:27.470
insanely evil.

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:35.290
And the final option was that there was something
else on God Valley that Garp and Roger could

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.980
not allow Rocks to take.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:40.290
But what could this magical treasure be?

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.250
**Pause** Uhh, maybe, but no.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:47.089
In all seriousness, it is actually highly
plausible that the world government’s devil

00:13:47.089 --> 00:13:52.030
fruits were kept on God Valley and this is
what Rocks Rocks was after all along.

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:57.910
We go into full detail of this theory in my
Best Rocks D. Xebec Theory video, but let’s

00:13:57.910 --> 00:13:59.970
briefly discuss the topic here.

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:04.610
Devil fruits are the source of the magical
powers in the One Piece world, so obviously

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.440
they are incredibly valuable.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:10.589
We know that the world government likes to
gather devil fruits, such as the Opi-Opi no

00:14:10.589 --> 00:14:15.279
Mi, and that government agents can sometimes
get strong devil fruits such as when these

00:14:15.279 --> 00:14:19.540
two secret agents were given their fruits
in Enies Lobby.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:26.440
So what if they have a large store of devil
fruits or even a devil fruit tree that used

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:28.310
to be on God Valley.

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:33.640
And while this is a theory, there is some
evidence to support it.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:40.589
For example, in chapter 999 Big Mom reminds
Kaido that she gave him his legendary devil

00:14:40.589 --> 00:14:46.290
fruit ON THE SAME DAY as the battle on God
Valley when the Rocks pirates fell to ruin.

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:50.399
What if she found it on God Valley during
the chaos of the battle?

00:14:50.399 --> 00:14:54.959
Similarly, we do not know where Whitebeard
got his legendary Tremor fruit, which is said

00:14:54.959 --> 00:14:58.630
to be capable of destroying islands.

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:04.420
We never see him use it until after the God
Valley incident, so what if he also found

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:06.279
his fruit during the battle.

00:15:06.279 --> 00:15:11.040
And remember how we said that Rocks’ toxic
crew dynamic would come back to bite him.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:15.810
Well, it is interesting to see that every
member of Rocks’ crew abandoned him at God

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:16.810
Valley.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:21.230
What if this crew, who didn’t really care
about their captain, got their strong devil

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:23.019
fruits and then just left.

00:15:23.019 --> 00:15:26.949
It also goes along with the idea that the
Rocks crew was formed to make one big score.

00:15:26.949 --> 00:15:33.819
So once they had their own powerful devil
fruits, the crew didn’t care to stick around.

00:15:33.819 --> 00:15:42.519
If all this is true, we have to imagine that
Rocks was after his own strong devil fruit

00:15:42.519 --> 00:15:44.579
so that he could take over the world.

00:15:44.579 --> 00:15:50.459
And I know we are super deep into theory territory
here, but let me make one last connection

00:15:50.459 --> 00:15:53.430
before we get back to things that we know.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:58.011
If Rocks was seeking a devil fruit to help
him conqueror the world, wouldn’t it make

00:15:58.011 --> 00:16:01.500
sense that he would want the strongest one
possible.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:06.240
Well, we are told that many people consider
a certain devil fruit to be the most dangerous

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:07.560
ability in history.

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:12.690
And that is the darkness fruit which was eaten
by Blackbeard.

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:18.430
What if Rocks was seeking this fruit on God
Valley and he didn’t fail, but that he actually

00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:22.740
got the fruit out into the world before he
died or disappeared forever.

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:28.389
And now let’s shift to Blackbeard, because
out of any character in the story he has the

00:16:28.389 --> 00:16:30.889
most direct connection to Rocks.

00:16:30.889 --> 00:16:32.990
Here are the facts.

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:39.110
Blackbeard named his ship the Saber of Xebec,
a clear reference to Rocks D. Xebec.

00:16:39.110 --> 00:16:46.100
The two pirates also appear to have the same
method of building crews based solely on strength.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:51.181
For example, Blackbeard gathered a large part
of his crew by having prisoners fight to the

00:16:51.181 --> 00:16:54.079
death and then only taking the strongest survivors.

00:16:54.079 --> 00:16:57.029
And Rocks’ crew was well known to fight
each other.

00:16:57.029 --> 00:17:00.410
Also, both crews seem to have a large number
of devil fruit users.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:04.610
Blackbeard has ensured that most members of
his crew have a devil fruit.

00:17:04.610 --> 00:17:08.760
With Rocks’ crew, we don’t know if all
of them had devil fruits, but Whitebeard,

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:13.839
Kaido, and Big Mom all eventually got over
powerful devil fruits.

00:17:13.839 --> 00:17:18.760
Blackbeard also cares a lot about dreams and
wants to conquer the world just like Rocks.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:24.839
They also are the only members of the D clan
who appear to be outright evil.

00:17:24.839 --> 00:17:27.780
Even their smiles are eerily similar.

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:30.950
They also both made this island their home
base.

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:36.020
This island has many names including Beehive,
Hachinosu, or simply Pirate Island.

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:41.530
This is where the Rocks pirates were formed,
and after the crew disbanded it was taken

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:43.900
over by the former Rocks pirate, Ochoku.

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:49.460
He was ruling Hachinosu until Blackbeard claimed
the island during the time skip.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:54.770
This incident also involved marine vice-admiral
Koby and was called the Rocky Port Incident.

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:59.590
And while we don’t know Ochoku’s exact
powers, he must have been strong because Blackbeard

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:04.799
said that he only was able to overthrow Ochoku
due to the assistance of Luffy’s friend

00:18:04.799 --> 00:18:08.630
and marine Vice-admiral Koby during the Rocky
Port Incident.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:11.960
And Blackbeard hasn’t changed much since
he took over the island.

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:17.280
With partying and drinking all around, it
is truly a lawless pirate paradise.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:20.980
And while Blackbeard currently rules this
island, there is some room to theorize that

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:23.940
Buggy the Clown may eventually make an appearance
on the island.

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:24.940
How, you ask?

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:30.590
Well remember that Buggy has long been chasing
the treasure of the former Rocks’ pirate,

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:31.590
Captain John.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:36.620
In chapter 233, we see Buggy searching for
the treasure on an island with an enormous

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:37.620
skull.

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:42.820
While this turned out to be the wrong island
with a giant skull, Hachinosu also has this

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:43.919
giant skull.

00:18:43.919 --> 00:18:49.100
So wouldn’t it make sense that Captain John’s
treasure was still on the island of the former

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:50.690
Rocks pirates?

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:55.590
This could eventually lead Buggy to this island.

00:18:55.590 --> 00:19:00.559
And who knows, maybe at the end of the story,
this could be Buggy’s home base.

00:19:00.559 --> 00:19:03.280
But enough of Buggy, let’s get back to Blackbeard.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:07.780
With all of the connections between Blackbeard
and Rocks, let’s explore this relationship

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:08.780
a bit further.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:12.770
We already discussed how Rocks could have
previously wanted Blackbeard’s devil fruit.

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:17.650
A common theory within the community is that
Rocks actually ate the Darkness fruit and

00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:20.809
his soul is still living inside of the fruit.

00:19:20.809 --> 00:19:22.850
Now before you call me crazy, let me explain.

00:19:22.850 --> 00:19:27.630
The Darkness fruit is said to be a strange
fruit compared to every other devil fruit.

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:32.360
It doesn’t work like a typical Logia fruit,
as it absorbs all attacks, instead of being

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:34.530
unaffected by common attacks.

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:40.390
Also, one of the main powers we see Blackbeard
use is to suck everything into a Black Hole

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:45.650
. If it can suck in people and buildings,
it isn’t that much of a stretch to think

00:19:45.650 --> 00:19:48.140
it could also contain a soul.

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:52.780
So could Blackbeard actually have a piece
of Rocks inside of him?

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:56.270
There is some evidence that it could be possible.

00:19:56.270 --> 00:20:00.200
We have multiple references of Blackbeard
possibly being multiple people.

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:04.320
Marco the Phoenix claims that he has a weird
body which might be the reason he was able

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:05.950
to eat two devil fruits.

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:09.250
Luffy and Zoro mention that he could be more
than one person.

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:13.799
And after a battle, apprentices Buggy the
Clown and Shanks discuss how Blackbeard is

00:20:13.799 --> 00:20:19.640
rumored to never sleep although this occurred
before Blackbeard obtained his Darkness fruit.

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:25.510
This could mean that he has multiple personalities
that come awake while the other or others

00:20:25.510 --> 00:20:26.510
sleep.

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:30.740
Whether this is true or not, there is certainly
some connection between the two.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:35.360
It could be that Blackbeard is somehow related
to Rocks, as Blackbeard was born two years

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:37.260
before the God Valley incident.

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:41.440
Another option is that Blackbeard inherited
Rocks’ will after reading a journal or something

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:46.680
left behind by Rocks, and Blackbeard to achieve
Rocks’ dream sometime in the near future.

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:52.320
And speaking of the future, Rocks’ influence
will undoubtedly impact the story later on.

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:57.420
If he is still alive, he will surely show
up to be an obstacle for the straw hats.

00:20:57.420 --> 00:21:03.200
Or if he is dead, we could learn more about
him from many different characters.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:08.000
The upper tier marines like Garp, Sengoku,
or the Commander in Chief, Kong, should certainly

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.750
know about him.

00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:14.549
Shanks and the other Roger pirates could know
about Rocks as well.

00:21:14.549 --> 00:21:18.190
And certainly Big Mom and Kaido know about
him, if they are still alive.

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:23.061
The five Elders and Imu should also know exactly
what happened to Rocks, and even Buggy, if

00:21:23.061 --> 00:21:27.800
he were to find Captain John’s treasure,
could discover clues about this mysterious

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:28.800
figure.

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:32.799
And I can imagine that at the same time we
find out more about Rocks D. Xebec, we will

00:21:32.799 --> 00:21:37.750
find out even more information about the most
mysterious and influential character in the

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:39.890
series: Joy Boy.

00:21:39.890 --> 00:21:44.450
Much like Luffy and Blackbeard are basically
opposites, the Joy Boy from the Void Century

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:48.120
and Rocks appear to have opposing roles in
the story.

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:52.120
Joy Boy brings liberation while Rocks wants
to conqueror and rule the world.

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:56.549
And this insane connection will undoubtedly
influence the future of the story.

00:21:56.549 --> 00:22:00.330
So, who is Joy Boy and what do we know about
this figure from the Void Century?

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:04.340
If you want to find out, you can watch this
video right here.

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:05.470
Shanks for watching.

